[32m+[m[32m# AION / Astra MCP Read-Only Interface Candidate v0.1.0[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mStatus: `IMPLEMENTED_CANDIDATE / READ_ONLY_INTERFACE`[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32mCanonical effect: `NONE`[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32mDeployment: `FALSE`[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32mNetwork exposure: `NONE`[m[41m  [m
[32m+[m[32mIndependent IV&V: `NOT_ACHIEVED`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis component is a deliberately small Model Context Protocol (MCP) gateway candidate for AION/Astra. It materializes the external-capability boundary without making MCP part of identity, memory truth, canonical state, or research authority.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Scope[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe first candidate is intentionally **tool-only and read-only**. It uses the stable MCP Python SDK `v2.0.0` and exposes only local stdio transport.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRegistered tools:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `aion_get_status`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `astra_get_status`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `memory_get_candidate`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `provenance_get_record`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `evidence_get_artifact`[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEvery tool is annotated as read-only, non-destructive, idempotent, and closed-world. No tool can write memory, mutate identity, alter canonical state, migrate a Runtime, execute shell commands, merge repository state, deploy, or perform unrestricted filesystem/network access.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Boundary model[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```text[m
[32m+[m[32mMCP_RETRIEVED != VERIFIED[m
[32m+[m[32mMCP_RESOURCE_OR_TOOL_OUTPUT != CANONICAL_STATE[m
[32m+[m[32mMCP_ACCESS != AUTHORITY[m
[32m+[m[32mMCP_SERVER_IDENTITY != AION_OR_ASTRA_IDENTITY[m
[32m+[m[32mMCP_RUNTIME_VIEW != RUNTIME_HANDLE[m
[32m+[m[32mMCP_RUNTIME_FINGERPRINT != RAW_LINEAGE_LOCATOR[m
[32m+[m[32mMEMORY_CANDIDATE_READ != ACCEPTED_FACT[m
[32m+[m[32mPROVENANCE_RECORD_READ != CLAIM_VERIFIED[m
[32m+[m[32mEVIDENCE_ARTIFACT_READ != CURRENT_SCOPE_VALIDATION[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAll returned payloads are wrapped in a `GatewayResult` envelope with:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `canonical_effect = NONE`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `accepted_as_fact = false`[m
[32m+[m[32m- explicit subject and found/not-found state[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe MCP layer therefore transports candidate information; existing recall, provenance, epistemic-integrity, writeback, and Human Owner authority gates remain responsible for acceptance or mutation decisions.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Provider boundary[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`SnapshotProvider` is the only source adapter contract in this candidate. The default `EmptySnapshotProvider` exposes no private state and returns an explicit `UNBOUND_PROVIDER` observation.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe optional `MaterializedRuntimeSnapshotProvider` can observe a **real AION Runtime and/or Astra Runtime at materialization time**, but it does not retain the Runtime object. It copies only an explicit allowlist of public Runtime status fields.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIndividual-runtime binding identifiers are not exposed raw. Each snapshot generates an ephemeral random 256-bit key, computes field-separated `HMAC-SHA256` fingerprints, and discards the key after materialization. The visible fingerprints are therefore intentionally **not stable across rematerialization** and are not intended as durable cross-session identifiers.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe materialized view deliberately excludes:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Runtime object references;[m
[32m+[m[32m- `SQLiteMemoryStore` handles or database paths;[m
[32m+[m[32m- `IndividualRuntimeStateStore` handles;[m
[32m+[m[32m- execution-engine handles;[m
[32m+[m[32m- raw `runtime_instance_id`, `memory_stream_id`, `event_lineage_id`, `canonical_state_reference`, and `genesis_root_id` values;[m
[32m+[m[32m- fingerprint keys;[m
[32m+[m[32m- `run_task`, `remember`, checkpoint, recovery, rollback, or migration capabilities.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe snapshot is point-in-time and must be explicitly rematerialized to observe later Runtime state. A boundary drift such as `automatic_canonical_writeback != DISABLED`, `subjectivity_conclusion != NOT_ESTABLISHED`, or `independent_ivv != NOT_ACHIEVED` fails closed instead of being surfaced automatically.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis design lets MCP distinguish the bound engineering Runtime within one materialized view without receiving a live capability handle, a raw lineage locator, or a durable cross-materialization tracking identifier. It does **not** independently verify identity or continuity.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMemory, provenance, GitHub, and local-environment adapters remain unbound in this Runtime-snapshot provider.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Transport[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe executable entry point is:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32maion-astra-mcp-readonly[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIt starts an **unbound** stdio MCP server only. Binding a materialized Runtime snapshot remains an explicit host-side construction step. HTTP/SSE hosting, authentication, TLS, remote deployment, Apps SDK widget UI, and mutating tools are outside this candidate.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Validation target[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe component tests use the MCP SDK's in-memory `Client` against the actual `MCPServer` object to verify:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- exact tool inventory;[m
[32m+[m[32m- safety annotations;[m
[32m+[m[32m- no MCP resources in the first candidate;[m
[32m+[m[32m- structured read-only result envelopes;[m
[32m+[m[32m- missing candidates fail closed without becoming facts;[m
[32m+[m[32m- actual `AIONRuntime` and `AstraRuntime` objects can be materialized into safe MCP projections;[m
[32m+[m[32m- raw lineage identifiers and local database paths are absent from the MCP-visible projection;[m
[32m+[m[32m- the provider retains no Runtime/store/state/execution handles;[m
[32m+[m[32m- Runtime fingerprints change across independent rematerializations;[m
[32m+[m[32m- unsafe Runtime boundary drift is rejected before exposure.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Provenance[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- MCP priority and authorization to continue into safe Runtime visibility for this cycle: `HUMAN_OWNER`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Read-only/tool-only architecture, one-way Runtime snapshot design, and implementation: `CHATGPT`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Existing AION/Astra Runtime binding and status contracts: repository pre-existing engineering artifacts.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Upstream MCP implementation contract: OpenAI Developers `build-chatgpt-app` installed skill plus the official Model Context Protocol Python SDK `v2.0.0` API.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `CODEX_CONTRIBUTION_THIS_CHANGE = NONE`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Non-claims[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- no canonical AION/Astra Runtime is established;[m
[32m+[m[32m- no identity continuity, subjectivity, consciousness, or autobiographical-memory conclusion is established;[m
[32m+[m[32m- no deployment authority is granted;[m
[32m+[m[32m- no private memory is published or bound;[m
[32m+[m[32m- no MCP host/client connection is evidence of relationship, identity, ownership, or authorization;[m
[32m+[m[32m- an ephemeral lineage fingerprint is only an opaque per-materialization engineering comparison value; it is not independent identity verification.[m
